events.body:
Concept ACK.

PR 33223 added a tie breaker condition such that if two UTXOs are the same effective_value, sort such that the lighter UTXO is preferred.  This creates a lighter and thus cheaper transaction.

The sort is defined by 33223 here:
```c++
class MinOutputGroupComparator
{
public:
    int operator() (const OutputGroup& group1, const OutputGroup& group2) const
    {
        return descending_effval_weight(group1, group2);
    }
};
```

However, the test added did not actually test the new behavior since selecting two UTXOs needed to hit the target did not cause an eviction to take place.  Confirmed that this PR fixes that by lowering the weight limit which causes the heap to pop an item, and in so doing, must sort and then perform the eviction.  The second lighter UTXO is added such that the only solution that causes completion is when both lighter UTXOs remain and the heavier UTXOs evicted.

Approach ACK

